<title>ITALY: FORECAST - Italy seen issuing 12.25 bln lire BOTs.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Italy seen issuing 12.25 bln lire BOTs.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is expected to issue some 12.25 trillion lire of short-term bills (BOT) at its mid-month auction against 13.75 trillion worth of paper maturing, a Reuter poll of analysts showed.</p>
<p>The forecasts ranged from a minimum 11.5 trillion lire worth to 12.75 trillion lire. The Treasury is also expected to issue its regular tranche of 2.5 trillion lire of zero coupon certificates (CTZ).</p>
<p>&quot;The Treasury will continue its policy of issuing less BOT bills than the amount expiring. The trend remains one of reducing short-term debt,&quot; one analyst said.</p>
<p>The Treasury will announce on Friday the amount of paper it will offer at the December 11 auction. Settlement date is December 16. Following are the analysts' forecasts (in trillion lire):</p>
<p>		     3-mo BOT  6-mo BOT  1-yr BOT  Tot BOT   CTZ</p>
<p>Maturing	    4.25	5.00	4.50	13.75     -</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------ Bank of America   3.75	4.75	4.25	12.75    2.00</p>
<p>Banca di Roma     3.50	4.50	4.00	12.00    2.00</p>
<p>Caboto		4.00	4.50	4.00	12.50    2.50</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan   3.50	4.00	4.00	11.50    2.50</p>
<p>BCI		   4.00	4.25	4.25	12.50    2.50</p>
<p>Credito Italiano  3.50	4.25	4.25	12.00    2.00</p>
<p>Banque Indosuez   3.75	4.75	4.25	12.75    2.50</p>
<p>Prometeia	   3.50	4.50	4.00	12.00    5.00*</p>
<p>*Forecast for whole month of December ------------------------------------------------------------ CONSENSUS	   3.75	4.50     4.00/25    12.25    2.50</p>
<p>============================================================ --Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
